g this sign outside of his family's  store the day after the attack on Pearl  Harbor masudo was born in California his  father had emigrated from Japan in the  1890s and opened the family store in  1916. win Lang took this photo in March  1942 the masudas had closed the store  following Roosevelt's executive order  they were placed in a concentration camp  in Arizona this photo taken around 1945  shows tatsuro with his family after they  were released from the camp thanks so  much to Jerry naruo tatsuro's nephew for  sharing these photos of the Masuda  family with us as always there's more in  the description including a link to the  collection of Lang's WRA photos with the  word impounded written on the print  which are held at the UC Berkeley  Bancroft library and a link to Satsuki  Ina's award-winning documentary about  her family's incarceration during World  War II from a silk cocoon
 

